{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPyX7xi5DjXF2wTwuAGD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The approve key is in, and `make lint test` passes. The report is written to `.ard/416/worker-engineer.md`.\n\n- **What `a` does:** `a` works on a selected row that is in the approval queue. It opens a confirm screen showing the number, title, worker role and plan link, all sanitised. Only `y` approves; Esc, Enter and any other key cancel.\n- **Approval:** the new `Effects.ApproveIssue` method runs `gh issue edit N --add-label ard:approved -R <repo>` with no shell. It is not on `github.Writer`, so the App client can't reach it. Under `--dry-run` it is recorded in the ledger and nothing runs.\n- **No `gh`:** if `gh` is missing or not logged in, the UI shows the issue URL and opens it in the browser. After a successful approval it wakes the triage loop.\n- **Queue:** I added an in-memory approval queue that the triage gate fills and clears. The snapshot carries it to the UI.\n- **Docs:** I added one sentence to the approval paragraph in `docs/proposal.md`.\n\nThe three existing UI golden files changed because the footer now includes `a approve`.\n\nLimitations, also listed in the report:\n- Under `--dry-run` the gate returns before queueing, so no rows are offered for approval there.\n- An issue that closes after it was queued stays in the queue until a restart.\n- `a` only acts on rows in the Issues list, which shows issues with activity today.\n\nI added tests for the effects, UI, servecmd, triage queue and snapshot changes, covering the acceptance cases."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":912,"cache_read_input_tokens":79471,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":912},"output_tokens":525,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_tran